{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1242777-beasts-in-the-hedge","id":1242777,"title":"Beasts in the Hedge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-04T13:10:17-07:00","id":1242777,"title":"Beasts in the Hedge","content":"Hey does a beast with the maze lair trait protect them from the confusion of the hedge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T17:08:32-07:00","id":1242824,"title":"","content":"The confusion of the Hedge is dramatically more involved than the mundane tilt of the Maze Trait and has relatively little to do with getting lost in normal terms, so probably not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T10:34:59-07:00","id":1242977,"title":"","content":"Yeah, CtL2 describes the Hedge as actively trying to mislead you, to the point that Hedge navigation uses the same subsystem as a chase scene. That said, Beasts supposedly warp the Hedge* with their presence, so I personally think it would be reasonable to give a Beast with Maze a +2 bonus to Hedge navigation rolls (equivalent to the Hedge Sense merit).<br /> <br /> *The Beast core refers to CtL1 p. 212-213 when describing this effect, using Lair instead of Wyrd. However, the new edition of Changeling replaces this subsystem with Hedgespinning, and I'm still thinking about how to apply this to Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T22:43:28-07:00","id":1243123,"title":"","content":"Well technically speaking a Beast's immunity to most Lair Traits will come best when they've performed an overlay of a Lair trait.<br /> So one could make a case that the Hedge will normally do things to screw up a Beast, but if a Beast overlay's their Lair for the Maze trait then the Hedge can't force itself through the Lair that way to screw with the Beghotten.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T23:59:04-07:00","id":1243135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1242777-beasts-in-the-hedge?p=1242824#post1242824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The confusion of the Hedge is dramatically more involved than the mundane tilt of the Maze Trait and has relatively little to do with getting lost in normal terms, so probably not.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mmm, I'd have to disagree. Dreams can be pretty disorienting by themselves, especially when you aren't aware that it's a dream. Adding to that is the fact this takes place in a nightmare landscape that is specifically tailored for invoking terror in those who trespass within it, and the Lair can be even more disorienting than usual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-06-2018, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T00:25:09-07:00","id":1243139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1242777-beasts-in-the-hedge?p=1243135#post1243135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Mmm, I'd have to disagree. Dreams can be pretty disorienting by themselves, especially when you aren't aware that it's a dream. Adding to that is the fact this takes place in a nightmare landscape that is specifically tailored for invoking terror in those who trespass within it, and the Lair can be even more disorienting than usual.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be true if we were talking about an intruder to the Lair, but we're talking about the Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}